 "response": "Drasti's budget is now **$2,497K**. I worked through all 1,600 records once by hand, with no independent re-check, so a slip in the arithmetic is possible.\n\n**Method**\n\n1. **Kept only Finance Office budget changes.** Messages from Sales, Engineering, Operations, PMO, Legal, Marketing, Facilities and vendors were ignored, as were Finance Office administrative notes such as receipts, audits and cost-center changes.\n2. **Started from #0001**, which set the budget to $2,300K.\n3. **Resolved each chain of withdrawals from the last link backwards.** A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so the item it targeted stands again. Two examples:\n   - #1570 withdraws #0162, which voids #0162. That makes #0122 effective, which voids #0055. That makes #0009 effective, so #0006 (+$158K) is withdrawn.\n   - #0201 withdraws #0015, so #0013 (\u2212$464K) stands.\n4. **Applied every remaining change in record order.** About 125 budget updates end up withdrawn. Among them are #0003, #0005, #0012, #0020, #0028, #0093, #0100, #0108, #0147 and #0230.\n\nANSWER: $2497K",
